`connectSum_homeo_of_homeos : Nonempty (X.Carrier ≃ₜ S3) → Nonempty (Y.Carrier ≃ₜ S3) → (compatible embeddings) → Nonempty ((connectedSum X Y eX eY).Carrier ≃ₜ S3)` where the embeddings are the transported south disks. The proof: connectedSum X Y (hX.symm∘downS3) (hY.symm∘downS3) ≃ connectedSum S3 S3 downS3 downS3 via quotientMapHomeo with e := hX.sumCongr hY on the punctured spaces?? Hmm — careful: the connected sum's carrier is Quot over PUNCTURED spaces — the punctured-of-disk homeos: puncturedOfDisk X.Carrier (hX.symm ∘ downS3) ≃ₜ puncturedOfDisk S3 downS3 via hX restricted... — {x : X // x ∉ e '' openBallInBall} → {y : S3 // y ∉ downS3 '' openBallInBall} via hX — well-defined: x ∉ (hX.symm∘downS3) '' openBall → hX x ∉ downS3 '' openBall (contraposition via hX). The homeo: ⟨hX x, not-in⟩ with inverse ⟨hX.symm y, ...⟩ — continuity via subtype_mk. This is a "puncturedHomeo" lemma:

```lean
def puncturedHomeo (e : X ≃ₜ Y) (fX : Ball3 → X) (fY : Ball3 → Y) (h : ∀ x, fY x = e (fX x)) :
    puncturedOfDisk X fX ≃ₜ puncturedOfDisk Y fY := ...
```
with the relation transport: connectSumRel(fX, fY) a b ↔ connectSumRel(gX, gY) (e a) (e b) — via the S2-witness transport: ∃ s, x.1 = fX s ↔ ∃ s, e x.1 = e (fX s) = fY s ✓.

